      "description": {
        "nodeId": "85:1256",
        "left": 826,
        "top": 277,
        "width": 424,
        "height": 269,
        "text": "A visual exploration inspired by Alfred Hitchcock and his approach to suspense. The project focuses on the tension between what is revealed and what remains hidden, using fragmented portraits, blur, shadow, and movement to create a sense of uncertainty and anticipation. Developed through a series of posters, a folded print piece, and a short moving-image experiment, the project translates Hitchcock’s cinematic language into a visual system across print and motion."
      },
