        "width": 564,
        "height": 242,
        "text": "An illustration exercise inspired by the visual language of Blexbolex. Using three selected words as a starting point, I created a series of illustrations based on word associations and visual contrasts. The images were made by hand using stencils and flat layers of color, with a consistent color hierarchy throughout the series. The project explores how simple shapes, limited color, and subtle irony can transform the meaning of familiar words."
